The super keyword is used to access the super class or parent class properties.
The syntax goes like super.<variable_name> or super.<method_name>.

Most commonly it is used under a non-static function which calls parent class properties.
Ex- void display(){
      this.age;
      super.age;
}

super keyword cannot be used in main() function because it is a static method and the super keyword cannot be used in a static type.
super keyword can only be used in a non-static method or a constructor.
